  "result": "The design document that specifies this mechanism is **`docs/design/event-bus.md`**, specifically section **DES-052 — Handler isolation via `Promise.allSettled`** (lines 105-121).\n\nThis section explicitly documents that `emit()` uses `Promise.allSettled` to collect all handler results, ensuring that:\n- If one handler throws, it's reported to error sinks but doesn't reject the `emit()` promise itself\n- A throwing subscriber never fails the originating write\n- A throwing subscriber never prevents sibling subscribers from running\n\nThe document emphasizes this is what makes the isolation true \"structurally rather than by convention.\"\n\nANSWER: docs/design/event-bus.md",
